{%- comment -%}
  Figma: Components Atoms / Block / Button (2173:9138): Button sm
  width   hug: as wide as the label | full: the full column width
  Landing block (private: the underscore keeps it out of every other section; only the Landing columns and tabs list it).
  Top and bottom padding are settings on the Figma Spacing scale (spacing/N = N x 4px), as pt-N / pb-N (Hendrik, 24 Nov).
  Width: Fit the label or Full width, on desktop and on mobile. The block is a flex box, so its height is the whole
  button: a block box around an inline button was text-trimmed to the label's capitals (11px for a 32px button), and
  the space to the next block was wrong in Chrome and Safari (Hendrik, 25 Nov).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign button_class = ''
  if block.settings.width_mobile == 'full'
    assign button_class = 'w-full'
  endif
  if block.settings.width == 'full'
    assign button_class = button_class | append: ' lg:w-full'
  else
    assign button_class = button_class | append: ' lg:w-auto'
  endif
-%}
<div class="landing-block flex min-w-0 pt-{{ block.settings.padding_top }} pb-{{ block.settings.padding_bottom }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
    {% render 'button', label: block.settings.label, href: block.settings.link, style: block.settings.style, size: 'sm', class: button_class %}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

